          "rationale": "Section 13 (p0078) is the only renewal mechanic: an initial 1-year term with automatic successive one-year renewal terms, exitable by either party on written non-renewal notice given no later than thirty (30) days before year end. The renewal term is 12 months (no multi-year auto-renewal) and the computed non-renewal notice window is 30 days, so the clause clears the fallback ceiling of 60 days and in fact matches the preferred renewal-length and 30-day opt-out elements. On pricing, no clause anywhere permits the Vendor to raise rates unilaterally at renewal: fees are fixed by the Exhibit A/B schedules, other-service fees are \"determined by the parties\" (p0045), amendments require a signed writing (p0081), and Section 6 (p0047) adds a one-year price freeze plus a most-favoured-rate undertaking in our favour, so the conditional price-uplift element is not engaged. Short of the preferred position the Vendor owes no 60-day pre-renewal reminder and there is no express CPI/3% cap on any post-year-one rate change; these are minor sub-elements noted here rather than redlined. The clause is acceptable at (indeed above) the fallback and benefits us on notice and rate protection, so we do not propose changes.",
